id: pm-s8cth5
title: "GH-1154: linked-test sandbox guard is command-shape inconsistent and undocumented"
description: "The linked-test add guard rejects direct node --test commands containing space-separated flags but accepts equivalent execution through sh -c, equals-spelled flags, or alternate runners. This makes the policy both bypassable and unnecessarily obstructive, while pm test help does not disclose content validation."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: agent-ux,"area:test-command",regression,sandbox-safety,trust
created_at: "2026-08-29T15:17:13.352Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-30T15:52:02.109Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-30T15:28:07.959Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-30T15:28:07.959Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "Define whether the linked-test add policy is a security boundary or an agent-safety nudge and encode that contract in the public SDK.; Normalize or safely inspect direct, sh -c, equals-spelled, package-manager, Node, and non-Node runner forms so equivalent capabilities cannot diverge accidentally.; Document command-content validation and safe recovery in pm test help and testing documentation.; Add negative and positive regression tests with exact 100/100/100/100 coverage and manual temporary-workspace acceptance."
definition_of_ready: "Read the complete pm-q813, pm-mlc3, and pm-ed28wi lineage plus the current src/cli/commands/test.ts and public SDK trust contracts before choosing the enforcement model."
goal: project management = context management
objective: "Make linked-test safety classification capability-aware, consistent across equivalent command forms, and discoverable before mutation."
value: "Agents can record precise acceptance tests without learning wrapper bypasses, while the intended workspace-data safety boundary remains enforceable and explainable."
impact: Removes a misleading shape-based guard that currently rewards less inspectable shell wrapping and surprises agents only after mutation.
outcome: "Equivalent linked-test executions receive equivalent safety classification, supported runners are intentionally defined, and pm test help documents the rule and safe recovery path."
why_now: GitHub issue #1154 was reported during PR #1149 closeout and reproduces on published pm 2026.8.28; documenting it now prevents the finding from being lost or misclassified as already-completed trust work.
parent: pm-n7rr
risk: high
confidence: high
severity: medium
environment: pm 2026.8.28 and 2026.8.21 on Linux/Node 24; linked-test mutation paths in CLI and SDK.
repro_steps: "Run pm test ITEM --add-json with node --test x.ts and observe refusal; then add sh -c wrapping, an equals-spelled Node flag, node test/x.test.ts, or pytest -k and observe acceptance."
resolution: "Replaced the shape-based intake refusal with a public SDK capability classifier, retained runtime tracker isolation and provenance enforcement, and documented the contract in CLI help and operator guidance."
expected_result: "Commands with equivalent execution capability are classified consistently, the policy's security boundary is explicit, and help reveals all content constraints before mutation."
actual_result: Direct node --test x.ts is refused while multiple equivalent or broader command forms are stored; the help contract does not mention command-content validation.
affected_version: 2026.8.28
component: sdk/test-trust-and-cli-test-intake
regression: true
customer_impact: Agents encounter a surprising refusal for the canonical Node test form and are nudged toward less inspectable wrappers that bypass the same guard.
