comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-29T15:17:13.352Z","harness:codex","Duplicate-check evidence: complete all-status keyword searches found closed pm-q813 for package-manager run-script wrappers, pm-mlc3 for package-manager flag prefixes, and pm-ed28wi for merge-time command provenance/trust. None owns capability-equivalent command normalization or missing pm test help disclosure. This issue recurs from pm-q813, is an incident in the broader trust boundary, and was discovered during pm-vwuidf exact-head closeout."
  "2026-08-30T15:28:04.347Z","harness:codex","Evidence: TDD first proved direct Node, shell-wrapped, Vitest, and package-manager forms diverged. The final tests cover 16 equivalent direct-runner spellings, sandbox-runner forms, non-runner forms, JSON intake, runtime isolation, and provenance. Manual acceptance in a temporary initialized workspace stored and ran a direct node --test command while proving injected PM_PATH and PM_GLOBAL_PATH, then imported the built SDK classifier. The workspace was removed afterward. Full coverage passed 8,144 tests at exact 100/100/100/100; pm test help is three estimated tokens below its ratcheted baseline."
  "2026-08-30T15:39:46.314Z","harness:codex","Delivery review: commit b031cd694 and PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1160 expose the SDK safety classifier, preserve runtime tracker isolation and provenance, and carry the complete local verification evidence."
  "2026-08-30T15:52:02.109Z","harness:codex","Review evidence: Greptile P2 correctly found inconsistent advisory classification for package test scripts. npm, pnpm, Yarn, and Bun test/test:* entrypoints now share direct-runner guidance with npx/bunx forms, with cross-runtime unit coverage."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-29T15:17:13.352Z","harness:codex","GitHub source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1154. Keep this item open and unclaimed until implementation is actively scheduled; PR #1149 only performs durable intake."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-29T15:17:13.352Z","harness:codex","String-token deny rules are not execution-capability boundaries: accepting sh -c around a refused command makes the bypass less inspectable than the direct form and creates counterproductive agent UX."
  "2026-08-30T15:28:04.818Z","harness:codex","Command spelling is not a security boundary. Classify capabilities for guidance, then enforce safety at the runtime boundary with isolated tracker roots and provenance-aware execution."
